          "text": "The pattern is consistent with a metal-rich, ordered interstitial structure derived from a close-packed Ti/Zr lattice. The strongest diagnostic reflections form an approximately hexagonal metric with \\(a_h\\approx4.88\\) \u00c5 and \\(c_h\\approx8.19\\) \u00c5. Splitting of the nominal hexagonal 110 family indicates an orthorhombically distorted or twinned derivative; however, the powder data alone do not uniquely determine the detailed Zr/Ti/O ordering.\n\nThe following is the primary chemically reasonable average structure. It has \\(Z=3\\), the required ZrTi\\(_2\\)O composition, and a close-packed layered metal arrangement with ordered interstitial oxygen. P1 is used deliberately because the exact ordering space group cannot be established reliably from the powder pattern alone.\n\n```cif\ndata_ZrTi2O_primary\n_audit_creation_method\n'Indexed and chemically constrained model from Cu Kalpha1 powder data'\n_chemical_name_common                 'zirconium dititanium oxide'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Zr3 Ti6 O3'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'ZrTi2O'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 3\n\n_cell_length_a                        4.882\n_cell_length_b                        4.882\n_cell_length_c                        8.190\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     120\n_cell_volume                          169.02\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P 1'\n_space_group_IT_number                1\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type                'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength          1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1 'x,y,z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nZr 0\nTi 0\nO  0\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\n\nZr1 Zr  0.000000  0.000000  0.166667 